WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:04.870
- My next guest is a true
wonder girl herself at 14.

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:06.700
She is only 14 years old.

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:08.760
She's already written, produced,

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:11.390
and financed her own animated short film.

00:00:11.390 --> 00:00:13.073
So sorry, all you adults out there

00:00:13.073 --> 00:00:15.660
that that was your dream, and
you still haven't done it,

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:18.140
and a 14-year-old just showed you up.

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:20.070
It's called "The Power of Hope",

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:22.410
and it's catching the
attention of Hollywood Studios.

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:23.446
Take a look.

00:00:23.446 --> 00:00:26.410
(upbeat music)
♪ We've got that power ♪

00:00:28.089 --> 00:00:33.089
♪ We've got that power ♪

00:00:33.301 --> 00:00:38.301
♪ We've got that power,
power, power of hope ♪

00:00:38.341 --> 00:00:43.341
♪ We've got that power,
power, power of hope ♪

00:00:46.917 --> 00:00:50.070
Please, y'all, give a big and warm welcome

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:53.640
to 14-year-old filmmaker Kalia Love Jones

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:55.074
and her father Gerald.

00:00:55.074 --> 00:00:57.860
(audience cheering)

00:00:57.860 --> 00:01:00.033
What's up?

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:04.620
Kalia, this film was
inspired by Michelle Obama.

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:06.070
It was a quote of hers.

00:01:06.070 --> 00:01:08.625
Can you tell me a little
bit, what was the quote?

00:01:08.625 --> 00:01:10.470
- Well Michelle Obama,

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:13.010
she's always been a
huge inspiration to me.

00:01:13.010 --> 00:01:15.760
And I just love, she
has such a big influence

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:18.250
on so many people including me.

00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:21.440
And I heard her speech, and in the speech,

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:23.240
she talked about overcoming obstacles.

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:24.860
And I really loved the message,

00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:26.640
and I wanted to send that out as well.

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:29.300
And I thought it was important
that the film was animated

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:32.870
because I wanted to reach
an audience that was my age.

00:01:32.870 --> 00:01:35.950
And also 'cause I just
love art and animation.

00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:39.730
- Yeah, no, I think that
was really clever and smart.

00:01:39.730 --> 00:01:40.810
Gerald, just to be clear,

00:01:40.810 --> 00:01:43.260
she did all of this on her own, right?

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:45.100
- Yeah, this was 100% Kalia.

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:47.330
She took the reins and ran with it.

00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:49.935
And I knew she was
passionate about filmmaking

00:01:49.935 --> 00:01:52.870
at an early age because she
would always be drawing,

00:01:52.870 --> 00:01:54.330
always do animation.

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:56.611
She'd ask for all these
apps to do it on her iPad.

00:01:56.611 --> 00:01:59.870
And then one thing I noticed
that I thought was unique

00:01:59.870 --> 00:02:01.870
is that she would watch an animated show

00:02:01.870 --> 00:02:03.060
and watch the credits,

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:05.307
and then come to us and
say, "What is this job?

00:02:05.307 --> 00:02:06.450
"What is that job?"

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:08.140
And she'd always have all these questions

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:10.530
that most kids would,
when the credits roll,

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:11.530
they just stop watching it.

00:02:11.530 --> 00:02:13.770
- I've never heard one kid ask that.

00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:14.603
That's awesome.

00:02:14.603 --> 00:02:16.230
- She's been passionate
about it the whole time.

00:02:16.230 --> 00:02:17.810
So when she came to us and said

00:02:17.810 --> 00:02:19.520
that she wants to do this film,

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:21.040
we knew she was serious.

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.870
And we didn't have any
experience in the industry.

00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:24.640
We don't know anybody in the industry.

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:27.577
So Kalia pretty much took
the reins and ran with it,

00:02:27.577 --> 00:02:29.550
and we just were cheerleading her on.

00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:30.520
- That's amazing.

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:33.590
Well, Kalia, it must've
been tough at times,

00:02:33.590 --> 00:02:35.480
like you have never done
this kind of thing before.

00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:37.657
Did you have any doubts
about finishing it?

00:02:37.657 --> 00:02:40.302
- Yeah, I definitely did
doubt myself at times.

00:02:40.302 --> 00:02:42.060
I felt scared.

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:45.290
I didn't like believe that
the movie would do well.

00:02:45.290 --> 00:02:48.291
And I still do doubt myself.

00:02:48.291 --> 00:02:50.710
- We all do, by the way.

00:02:50.710 --> 00:02:52.750
- I still do doubt myself and get nervous

00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:57.110
talking to a lot of people and
getting a lot of attention,

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:59.530
but I just have to keep going.

00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:00.363
- Yeah.

00:03:00.363 --> 00:03:02.260
Well mentors are important,

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:05.100
and I have some news for Kalia.

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:08.530
Her film caught the attention
of some pretty powerful women.

00:03:08.530 --> 00:03:10.320
Let's get them in here.

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:11.420
Kalia, why don't you say hi

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:13.800
to "Wonder Woman" star Gal Gadot

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:17.840
and director Patty Jenkins,
who just so happens

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:21.440
to be the highest grossing
female director in history.

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:24.369
Both actually watched your short film.

00:03:24.369 --> 00:03:26.340
And Gal, I'll start with you.

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:28.300
What impresses you about this young woman?

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:30.190
I am so impressed by her.

00:03:30.190 --> 00:03:31.023
- You know what?

00:03:31.023 --> 00:03:34.930
It blows... You just blew
my mind with this film.

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:36.790
It's so... I would never,

00:03:36.790 --> 00:03:39.360
if someone would have
shown it to me before,

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:42.960
I would never imagine that a 14-year-old

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:44.520
can produce such a story.

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:48.490
But more than anything, the fact

00:03:48.490 --> 00:03:53.490
that your inner compass is so in-tune

00:03:53.690 --> 00:03:58.570
with all the good things
in the world blows my mind

00:03:58.570 --> 00:04:01.920
because children in your
age, usually they care

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:05.110
about social media and
this and that and friends.

00:04:05.110 --> 00:04:09.710
And they don't think about
the greatness of the world.

00:04:09.710 --> 00:04:14.050
And you did, you do, and
this is beautiful to see.

00:04:14.050 --> 00:04:18.330
And I have no doubt you're
gonna fulfill all of your dreams

00:04:18.330 --> 00:04:21.440
because you're talented,
you're passionate,

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:23.210
you're a hard worker,

00:04:23.210 --> 00:04:26.820
and you don't let anything
or anybody stops you.

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:30.700
And it just inspiring for me to see you.

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:33.440
So thank you so much for your work.

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:34.970
- Oh, my god, that was Wonder Woman.

00:04:34.970 --> 00:04:38.780
I'm just saying, Wonder Woman
just like, "You're cool."

00:04:38.780 --> 00:04:40.020
What about you, Patty?

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:41.360
'Cause you started at a young age.

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:42.193
You loved cameras.

00:04:42.193 --> 00:04:44.250
You loved it, you knew at a young age.

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:45.150
But what about this?

00:04:45.150 --> 00:04:47.280
At 12 years old, she started this.

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:50.480
- Yeah, I just want to
say congratulations to you

00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:55.240
because I was so impressed
whatever the age is.

00:04:55.240 --> 00:04:57.080
There was so much that I relate with there

00:04:57.080 --> 00:04:59.160
because I very much have the same mission

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:02.010
of trying to make things
that put a message

00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:04.490
that's very personal and
might inspire other people.

00:05:04.490 --> 00:05:06.680
But even the way that you
say you chose animation

00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:08.830
because you wanted it to be something fun

00:05:08.830 --> 00:05:11.020
and that people can take in, so smart.

00:05:11.020 --> 00:05:14.290
Listen, I felt like your
story was a self portrait

00:05:14.290 --> 00:05:17.350
of a lot of people, but definitely myself.

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:19.520
It really, I had so much adversity.

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:21.130
I still have so much adversity.

00:05:21.130 --> 00:05:22.450
I doubt myself.

00:05:22.450 --> 00:05:24.190
I don't know that I'm
making the right decision.

00:05:24.190 --> 00:05:26.160
But you're right, that beautiful speech,

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:28.400
and putting one foot in front of the other

00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:30.255
and where you can make it to that way.

00:05:30.255 --> 00:05:33.790
I can't believe I've made it where I have.

00:05:33.790 --> 00:05:35.970
And I know that I'm not gonna...

00:05:35.970 --> 00:05:38.050
I know that I'm going to see you again

00:05:38.050 --> 00:05:41.140
if you keep putting one foot
in front of the other too

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:42.436
because you have everything,

00:05:42.436 --> 00:05:45.331
you have the drive and the
will and the good heart

00:05:45.331 --> 00:05:49.115
that you're really... That's
gonna guide you a long way

00:05:49.115 --> 00:05:51.530
if you continue to want to do this.

00:05:51.530 --> 00:05:52.363
- Yeah.

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:54.310
Are you freaking out?

00:05:54.310 --> 00:05:55.464
I'm freaking out for you.

00:05:55.464 --> 00:05:56.453
- [Gerald] I'm freaking out.

00:05:56.453 --> 00:05:57.738
- You're freaking out, no, you're not.

00:05:57.738 --> 00:05:58.938
- I'm like, "Don't cry."

00:05:59.870 --> 00:06:01.389
- That's amazing.
- I'm just so proud of her.

00:06:01.389 --> 00:06:02.610
- I know, and it's amazing to think

00:06:02.610 --> 00:06:04.173
you brought her to this college campus

00:06:04.173 --> 00:06:05.100
so that you could find animators

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:07.460
that came from her walking up
to these strangers to get help

00:06:07.460 --> 00:06:11.400
to now sitting on this show
talking to Gal and Patty.

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:13.080
It's amazing what life can do,

00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:17.220
especially when you focus
not on just the destination.

00:06:17.220 --> 00:06:18.870
You focus on that journey
of getting it done

00:06:18.870 --> 00:06:19.920
and doing what you love.

00:06:19.920 --> 00:06:22.220
That's when I think you win every time.

00:06:22.220 --> 00:06:24.780
And I feel like you're
one of those stories.

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:26.400
And I thank you so much
for coming on this show,

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:29.200
and thank you for sharing
your beautiful short film.

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:30.520
Yeah?

00:06:30.520 --> 00:06:32.210
- Kelly, can I interrupt
with one more thing?

00:06:32.210 --> 00:06:33.206
- Yes.

00:06:33.206 --> 00:06:35.750
- I'm so sure that I'm
gonna see her again,

00:06:35.750 --> 00:06:38.370
but I don't want to miss the
chance to make sure that I do

00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:39.990
because I really like to meet

00:06:39.990 --> 00:06:42.510
and inspire all young filmmakers.

00:06:42.510 --> 00:06:44.500
So I wanted to know, would
you come and visit me

00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:47.060
on the set of the next "Star Wars" movie?

00:06:47.060 --> 00:06:47.893
- What?

00:06:49.105 --> 00:06:51.397
That just happened!

00:06:51.397 --> 00:06:53.187
That was not planned.
- Oh, my god.

00:06:53.187 --> 00:06:55.612
- She's just awesome all on her own.

00:06:55.612 --> 00:06:57.503
That was not planned.
- Yeah.

00:06:57.503 --> 00:06:59.430
- Oh, my gosh.

00:06:59.430 --> 00:07:01.210
Oh, my gosh, are you down?
- Yes.

00:07:01.210 --> 00:07:02.970
- If you need a chaperone-
- I'm chaperoning.

00:07:02.970 --> 00:07:06.330
- If he's busy, if he's busy, I got you.

00:07:06.330 --> 00:07:08.580
I can take you, I'll help you out.

00:07:08.580 --> 00:07:10.330
No, that was so cool, Patty.

00:07:10.330 --> 00:07:11.880
That was a beautiful thing.

00:07:11.880 --> 00:07:13.480
And it is, it's actually funny

00:07:13.480 --> 00:07:15.150
'cause we do a lot of that on this show.

00:07:15.150 --> 00:07:17.290
We have women, we have call
it A Whole Lot of Woman.

00:07:17.290 --> 00:07:18.550
We have this whole segment

00:07:18.550 --> 00:07:19.480
called A Whole Lot of Woman,

00:07:19.480 --> 00:07:22.270
and we have people in Patty's
position that are so powerful

00:07:22.270 --> 00:07:24.850
and have earned it and
have worked their way up

00:07:24.850 --> 00:07:28.270
and are trying to help younger
women achieve what they have.

00:07:28.270 --> 00:07:29.840
And it's so funny that that just happened,

00:07:29.840 --> 00:07:30.840
and we didn't plan that.

00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:32.560
It just, she's just awesome.

00:07:32.560 --> 00:07:34.120
And that was really cool.

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:36.553
Anyway, I'm freaking out, all right.

